        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> thank you for making restart more reliable :) i am curious why this only affects restart though, i.e. i would expect the solution to live in the session logic, not restart-specific. if there is a reason for this, would be helpful if the commit msg explains it.\r\n\r\nGood point. There is no particular reason for this to be `restart`-specific. I put the workaround there because `restart` has an explicit post-session-load step, but the underlying failure can happen during any session restore if a `BufAdd` handler loads a buffer before it is edited.",
